[K. THE R11 CEILING GATE — 'if it sounds usable at 100 %, that is not what we want']
        METRIC (boosts): MSD = max |transfer| in dB over the 96 log bins, measured on the
               OUTPUT spectrum of white noise through the real 128-sample block path.
        METRIC (cuts): a coherent SINE at the notch centre — a band-averaged spectrum
               physically cannot see a hole narrower than its own analysis band.
        THRESHOLDS, defended: a mixing EQ tops out at 12-18 dB, and every console ever
               built tops out at 16. 28 dB from ONE knob at Amount 100 % is already past
               all of them; 55 dB at Amount 200 % is a factor of 560 on one band. A cut
               must reach -60 dB: at that depth the band is GONE, not 'reduced'.
        CONTROL (a plain, obvious +12 dB Low shelf): MSD = 12.4 dB
